; LowLevelPort0 -- what GLQuake leaves on the mouse port (lowlevel.library):
; after 1.1 (GLQuakeA) port 0 stays in autosense; after the new build it is
; locked to mouse mode. JoyPeek 0 reads it five times and prints the type
; lowlevel reports. 1.1 first: the new build's exit overrides its state.
; VBList shows the VBlank servers (any SetJoyPortAttrs/ReadJoyPort(0) swaps
; gameport.device's for lowlevel's, until the next boot).
; Needs: gmake glquake QCPU=040 glquake-data rgl-lib, DEV:Quake/GLQuakeA,
; DEV:Test/VBList, DEV:Test/JoyPeek.
; LIMIT 1500
FailAt 1000
Wait 12
Echo "=== machine ===" >DEV:Test/auto.log
CPU >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Version lowlevel.library FULL >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== VBlank servers at boot ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
DEV:Test/VBList >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Stack 1000000
Delete >NIL: DEV:Test/nullb-#?
Echo "=== GLQuakeA (1.1) demo1 ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunNullB GLQuakeA demo1 400
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/nullb-demo1.done
Search DEV:Test/nullb-demo1.log "Port 0" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Search DEV:Test/nullb-demo1.log "fps" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== port 0 after 1.1 ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
DEV:Test/JoyPeek 0 >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Delete >NIL: DEV:Test/nullb-#?
Echo "=== GLQuake040 (new) demo1 ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunNullB GLQuake040 demo1 400
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/nullb-demo1.done
Search DEV:Test/nullb-demo1.log "Port 0" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Search DEV:Test/nullb-demo1.log "fps" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Search DEV:Test/nullb-demo1.log "Port 1:" NONUM >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== port 0 after the new build ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
DEV:Test/JoyPeek 0 >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== VBlank servers at the end ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
DEV:Test/VBList >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== done ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
